{
  "assembly_notes": "Crossed scissor lift jack. One rigid lift_base root carries the frame rails, the pivot lugs and the actuator. Each of scissor_stage_count stages is a real X: arm_a is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of that stage's host (the base for stage 0, the previous lift_deck otherwise) and is the stage's only independent joint; arm_b is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of arm_a at the cross pivot with mimic multiplier -2; the stage's lift_deck is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of arm_b at arm_b's upper pin with mimic multiplier +1. Those two mimics are what make the linkage a closed scissor inside a URDF tree: the deck stays exactly level and at a fixed y while its height is 2*a*sin(theta), arm_a's upper roller slides under the deck and arm_b's lower roller slides along the host rail. The topmost deck carries the deck_fitting. Four component slots vary without touching the mechanism: arm_style (link section), frame_style (base frame section), deck_fitting (platform load interface) and drive_unit (actuator input, a REVOLUTE lever mounted outboard of the rails). deck_len_m, deck_width_m and arm_span_ratio are independent continuous parameters that derive arm length, per-stage lift, slider travel, rail spacing, plate x stations and pin lengths; palette is non-core.",
